{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# End-to-End RAG System Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `Chunk` - the record carried through all stages (extends lesson 64's shape with a chunk_index and source doc_id)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `Chunker` - selects a strategy from lesson 64 (default recursive split)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `HybridIndex` - bundles BM25 + dense + RRF from lesson 65."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `Rewriter` (optional) - picks one of HyDE, multi-query, decomposition from lesson 67 by query length and presence of conjunctions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `Reranker` - the trained cross-encoder from lesson 66, with a smaller fixture training set so it converges in seconds."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `Generator` - the deterministic mock generator with citations and refuse-on-low-confidence."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `Pipeline` - composes the five stages with a `query(question)` method that returns `Result(answer, top_k, latency_ms_per_stage)`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `run_demo()` - ingests the corpus, runs three fixture queries, runs the eval, prints results, sets exit code by threshold."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The output is one printed query trace, the full eval table, and a final pass/fail status. Returns exit code 0 on the fixture."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Add a per-query strategy selector inside the rewriter: heuristics from lesson 67 (length, conjunctions, jargon ratio) pick HyDE, multi-query, or decomposition.\n2. Add a real LLM call for the generator behind an env flag. Default to the mock. Measure the latency delta.\n3. Extend the demo to take a `--corpus path` flag that loads a real corpus. Re-run the eval and the threshold check.\n4. Add a `--strategy` flag to the chunker. Measure each strategy's contribution to end-to-end recall.\n5. Add a streaming generator interface and feed it into the eval. Confirm that faithfulness is computed on the final string and not on the streamed prefix."
      ]
    }
  ],
